  "lesson": {
    "slug": "research-questions-literature-searching",
    "title": "Research Questions & Literature Searching",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "From Observation to Searchable Question",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Once you've noticed a problem worth investigating, the next step is converting that observation into a rigorous, searchable question. A vague question like "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "\"How do we improve treatments?\"",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " or "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "\"How do we make learning easier?\"",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " yields too much irrelevant information to be useful. You need precision \u2014 whether your focus is inside the treatment vault or inside the classroom."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Problem Statement",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Before asking a question, define the problem. A "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "problem statement",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " clearly identifies the gap between the current state and a desired state, and it's what justifies why a project is worth doing in the first place."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Clinical example:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Current state",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 prostate patients frequently experience delays from inadequate bladder filling on daily CBCT. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Desired state",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 patients maintain consistent bladder volumes, reducing table time. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The gap",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 it's unclear whether a standardized hydration protocol beats standard verbal instructions at maintaining target volumes."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Educational example:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Current state",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 students struggle to visualize 3D anatomy from 2D textbook diagrams. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Desired state",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 students demonstrate strong spatial awareness before entering clinic. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The gap",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 whether VR-based training systems improve clinical readiness compared to traditional didactic learning."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The PICO Framework",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "To bridge the gap, formulate a specific question. "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "PICO",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is the gold standard for breaking a broad topic into a testable inquiry. Originally built for clinical medicine, its logic applies just as well to educational and administrative research."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
